# Environment
.env
.env.*

# Jolli / Claude
#
# `.jolli/` holds two very different things, so it is excluded entry-by-entry rather
# than as a directory. Everything in it is per-developer state — `jollimemory/` carries
# sessions, cursors and queues, written per worktree with absolute local paths — and
# none of that is a team artifact.
#
# The one exception is `agents.json`: a decision somebody made about *this* repository
# (its verify gate, base branch, directory layout), which a teammate cannot regenerate
# and therefore must be committed. The ORDER matters and so does the trailing `*`: a
# bare `.jolli/` would stop git descending into the directory at all, and a negation
# cannot re-include a file whose parent was never entered.
#
# Note the anchoring, which is the subtle half. The old `.jolli/` had no internal slash,
# so it matched a `.jolli` directory at ANY depth — including `cli/.jolli/`, which is
# also per-developer state. Adding `/*` anchors the rule to the root and would have
# quietly exposed the nested ones, so they are re-excluded explicitly below.
/.jolli/*
!/.jolli/agents.json
*/.jolli/
*/**/.jolli/
.claude/
.kiro/
.gemini/
.agents/
.cursor/
.codex/
.opencode/
.devin/
.qoder/
.workbuddy/
.reasonix/
.playwright-cli/
.playwright-mcp/
.codegraph/
# Claude MCP server config — written per-worktree with an absolute local path
# (jolli install → registerMcpInClaude), so it must never be committed.
.mcp.json
# Per-developer Claude/agent hooks overrides (references $HOME paths).
settings.local.json
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.iml
**/dist/
**/coverage/
**/node_modules/
**/*.vsix
.superpowers/
# Marketplace zips. publish-zip.sh writes $HOME/Desktop by DEFAULT; this covers the
# repo-relative path it resolves when given an explicit argument
# (`publish-zip.sh outputs/jolli-codex-plugin-marketplace-1.0.0.zip`).
/outputs/

# Generated codicon assets (copied from node_modules at build time)
vscode/assets/codicons/

# Generated knowledge-graph viz assets (copied from cli/src/graph/assets at build time)
vscode/assets/graph/

# Local pre-PR review state (per-developer scratch)
.claude/review-findings/

# Personal notes
notes.md

# claude-plugin ships these as part of the plugin package, but they are caught by
# broad ignores above (.mcp.json at repo root; SKILL.md in the user's global
# gitignore). Re-include them so the plugin is committed complete.
!/claude-plugin/plugins/**/.mcp.json
!/claude-plugin/plugins/**/SKILL.md

# codex-plugin, same reason. It needs one rule claude-plugin does not: its
# marketplace lives under `.agents/`, and that whole DIRECTORY is ignored above
# (Jolli writes `.agents/skills/` into user repos). Git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded — it never descends into it — so the
# directory has to be un-excluded first, before any pattern inside it can match.
# No `.mcp.json` rule: unlike claude-plugin, this plugin deliberately ships none
# (MCP is registered into ~/.codex/config.toml so the host launches the server with
# the session cwd — see cli/src/install/mcp/HostRegistrars.ts).
!/codex-plugin/.agents/
!/codex-plugin/plugins/**/SKILL.md
